      "text": "**Yes—given your asthma, I’d stay indoors in Kuala Lumpur tonight if you can.** On **Saturday, October 17**, one current citywide estimate put air quality around **AQI 165 (“unhealthy”)**, though readings vary by location and source. That’s enough to avoid outdoor exercise and keep time outside brief. ([airindex.today](https://airindex.today/en/air-quality-index-kuala-lumpur-1735161?utm_source=openai))\n\nKeep windows closed if it’s comfortable, use air conditioning with the fresh-air intake closed if available, and follow your asthma action plan; keep your reliever inhaler handy. If you need to go out, take it easy and leave if you start coughing, wheezing, or feeling tight-chested. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/sites/default/files/2023-03/air-quality-guide-for-particle-pollution_0.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf your breathing becomes severe, you can’t speak comfortably, or your reliever isn’t helping, seek urgent medical care.",
